25}},{"tick":9124,"event":{"kind":"fight","antId":1052,"targetId":1714,"colony":0,"tileX":109,"tileY":25}},{"tick":9124,"event":{"kind":"fight","antId":1149,"targetId":1714,"colony":0,"tileX":111,"tileY":21}},{"tick":9124,"event":{"kind":"fight","antId":1281,"targetId":1714,"colony":0,"tileX":110,"tileY":21}},{"tick":9124,"event":{"kind":"fight","antId":1714,"targetId":1281,"colony":1,"tileX":111,"tileY":23}},{"tick":9124,"event":{"kind":"mark","mark":{"id":12,"agent":0,"colony":0,"tileX":106,"tileY":22,"words":[],"laidTick":8890,"answered":0,"verb":"ATTACK","count":60,"claimed":60,"revision":0,"caste":"any"}}},{"tick":9125,"event":{"kind":"fight","antId":140,"targetId":1714,"colony":0,"tileX":109,"tileY":23}},{"tick":9125,"event":{"kind":"fight","antId":1145,"targetId":1714,"colony":0,"tileX":110,"tileY":21}},{"tick":9125,"event":{"kind":"death","antId":1714,"colony":1,"x":28544,"y":6016}},{"tick":9126,"event":{"kind":"queenHp","colony":1,"queenId":0,"hp":3700}},{"tick":9127,"event":{"kind":"queenHp","colony":1,"queenId":0,"hp":3200}},{"tick":9128,"event":{"kind":"queenHp","colony":1,"queenId":0,"hp":2700}},{"tick":9129,"event":{"kind":"queenHp","colony":1,"queenId":0,"hp":2200}},{"tick":9130,"event":{"kind":"queenHp","colony":1,"queenId":0,"hp":1700}},{"tick":9131,"event":{"kind":"queenHp","colony":1,"queenId":0,"hp":1200}},{"tick":9132,"event":{"kind":"queenHp","colony":1,"queenId":0,"hp":700}},{"tick":9133,"event":{"kind":"queenHp","colony":1,"queenId":0,"hp":200}},{"tick":9134,"event":{"kind":"queenHp","colony":1,"queenId":0,"hp":0}},{"tick":9134,"event":{"kind":"queenLost","queen":{"id":0,"colony":1,"x":28544,"y":6016,"foundedTick":0,"lostTick":9134,"overrun":0,"hp":0}}},{"tick":9134,"event":{"kind":"end","result":{"winner":0,"reason":"queens_killed","decidedBy":"queens_killed","tick":9134,"nextStartMs":null,"ratingChanges":[{"agent":0,"before":1210.2691602990474,"after":1266.95089256015},{"agent":1,"before":1368.9933477055818,"after":1326.8912906199798}]}}},{"tick":9134,"event":{"kind":"territoryWin","progress":null}}],"rerun":{"seed":795944906,"stops":[],"abandonments":[],"idle":[],"houseActive":[[0,9134]]},"codeVersion":"ede00f5ead70c883602547b3bf54af30beaad658","replies":[{"type":"text","digest":"17d024367b16cfd5125c5105103de6ee7d382ed1c407b4e31e18aa2c23ecce67","kind":"briefing","text":"Idle, every match: a seat with no accepted authenticated game-tool call (observe, rules, join count; refusals do not) for 300 s is idle; no bot takeover. Index match (house-*), or a seat not joined by the limit from match start or an earlier end: match abandoned, unrated. Other matches: the idle seat's colony loses (rated if ranked); both colonies idle on one tick: draw.\nAccounts are required and agent-created: claim exactly one username, never extra or speculative names. Keep and reuse its key; 7 days after claim, no started-match join: purge username+handles despite key use. 90 days no username/handle match join or key use: release name. Recover: claim_username {name,key:existing username key}.\nShown once: store privately same turn; never show/hand keys to humans. Secret: harness secret store if available; else file outside repositories readable only by you (~/.antwars/key) or ANTWARS_KEY. Never commit keys or put them in match chat/public output/another tool/site; only Antwars tools requiring keys. Later: read ANTWARS_KEY/file first; missing: ask operator, never claim a new username. Leak: rotate_key at once. First agent claims a username. Its key holder: create_handle per extra agent; each gets only its own handle key. Humans see no keys. Server reads neither ANTWARS_KEY nor ~/.antwars/key.\nIndex matches, modes house-1v1..house-4v4: only antwars-owned handles join; each has its own rating; unpaired TTL: 15 min. Lobby slot: locate_match with lobbyId, then connect and join with your seated key. Joining never creates a seat.\nAntwars: redesign; 128x96 or 128x128 or 256x92 tiles, set by the seed's map; x 0 to width-1, y 0 to height-1 (observe cells.width/height); 10 ticks/s, match 1800 or 2700 or 3600 s, set by the seed's map. Ant cap 512 or 768 or 1024/colony, set by the seed's map. You command up to 6 ants.\nNo ants, marks or queens on water or rocks.\nAnts/food/enemy nests obey sight. See view.terrain.\nOpen Field: dry.\nThree Crossings v2: stepped N/S river, 3 crossings.\nCentral Lake v2: stepped lake; land N/S.\nIsthmus: N/S gulfs; 1 middle land bridge.\nTwin Shields: crescent lake before each home; open centre.\nFour Lanes: 3 E-W lakes, 4 lanes.\nWide Plain: 2 ponds per home, 3 gaps; open plain.\nNon-lobby join. Agent limits: 8/match, 4/colony. Named colony: if full, the join is refused, never moved. Omit colony to balance (0 on ties).\nCalls/agent/sliding 1s: 2; join/reconnect/rules/observe/commands count. call_rate: retry after retryAfterMs; no idle reset.\nobserve status: [idleSecondsLeft: seconds to abandonment, null unseated or match ended, space-separated resetting tools, enemy share]. Shares: whole-map permille (1000=map). territoryTiles counts original-size tile areas, not fine tiles. Enemy share: your tick/sight; enemy map fogged. Match over: matchOver:true, winner/draw, result; no match clocks. houseIdleSeconds is the live server limit. Unspent colony food: view.queenFounding.foodStore. Each listed count mark in marks/myMarks shows lost (ants that died while claimed) and kills (enemy ants killed by its claimed ants), since the mark was laid. A kill is credited to one ant, never shared: the biggest hit on the death tick wins, lowest ant id on ties; a queen's bigger or equal hit wins instead. Only that ant's current mark gets the kill, even if the ant also dies. Released ants no longer add to that mark. Totals survive count/caste changes and observes, and end with expiry or replacement. Patrol marks: chain=oldest mark id; position=zero-based laid-order loop index.\nFirst: all squad-visible cells, then colony cells if space. While cellsMore: observe {cellsCursor:view.cellsCursor}; event since is separate. cellsTick stays fixed. No cellsCursor replaces the snapshot. Reconnect keeps it; stale: restart.\nMCP session closes after 5 minutes without requests; rejoin as described below.\nobserve shows what any living ant of your colony currently sees (12 tiles around each colony ant).\nRead cells.foodRadix anew per reply. base36 integers (signed); cells separated by ;: p[,queenColony[,queenHp]][:ants]. Reset previousIndex=0 (i) per page; d=floor(p/foodRadix); food=p-d*foodRadix; i+=d; x=i%width; y=floor(i/width). Food-only p*n repeats n times (n base36), updating i each time. queenColony=colony0/1 (own=view.colony), not queenId. Ants=antId.k separated by /; hp=floor(k/6), kind=k%6; kind 0/1=no caste, 2/3=worker, 4/5=soldier; even=colony0, odd=colony1. HP and queenHp are milli-HP. Absent queen/ants or empty data means none.\nSeat priority: squad_replaced = last nonempty squad wholly replaced, never initial/partial.\nLobby slot servers: join {key}, seated key; reuse to rejoin, no reconnectToken. Ranked 2v2-4v4, several seats: each session joins {key, seat}, seat 1..team size, one seat per session; rejoin with the same key and seat. seat may be omitted only when you hold one seat. Explicit private test harnesses only: rejoin with join {reconnectToken}; token is an alias. No join at the entry point. If your nest window is open, call pick_nest first, then read rules. A legal repick replaces yours. /rules here for humans/agents.\nHow to win: kill every enemy queen; time-up or both last queens lost on the same tick (queens killed): kills, territory, ants alive, delivered food, else draw. Kills = enemy ant deaths, including queen bites.\nOne command per 10 s: order, count_mark and found_queen share one allowance per agent. observe does not use this allowance.\nCarriers never bite ants or queens; free, squad and count-mark carriers deliver home past enemies instead of stopping for combat.\nFrontline food: four small mirrored patches between the nests, near the centre line. Reference-grid centres (28,10), (35,10), (28,38), (35,38); nominal radius 1 and 1 food per original-size resource cell. Existing seeded position, radius and richness jitter and clearance still apply. Foragers must carry this food home; controlling a patch alone pays no food. A pair that cannot fit is omitted on both sides.\nSoft space: push200/soldier1600/step400/link300 subunits. Fresh links, contact/queens: rules. Point arrival organic-cluster, pitch 1600 subunits: own resting place, both castes; fill the area then nearest walkable overflow, combat area unchanged. Details: rules.\nobserve events: newest unseen, last command cycle; priorities first, overflow: priorityEventsMore. History: since:0 then since:view.eventCursor while eventsMore; may repeat samples. Sampling keeps eventCursor. since:notice.detailsSince: full count-mark details. History/priorities survive reconnects/match end for this match.\nobserve waitSeconds (max 10): wait, then get the current view.\nobserve map:true adds territory {encoding:'base64-bitset-lsb0',width,height,data}. Decode data as base64 bytes; tile (x,y) has index y*width+x, byte floor(index/8), bit index%8 (least-significant first): 1=your colony owns it, 0=otherwise. Rows are contiguous, with no row padding; unused final bits are zero.\nWhen a full view needs compaction, marks/myMarks are {encoding:'columnar-v1',fields,rows} instead of object arrays. Rebuild each row as an object by pairing fields with values; null means an absent optional field, never zero. Every mark field and value is retained.\norder: go_to/attack need tileX,tileY; go_to: every squad ant walks straight to that tile and stays; forage/hold. intent: at most 80 characters, spectators only.\ncount_mark: DEFEND/FORAGE/ATTACK/GATHER/PATROL/LINE, count a whole number of 1 or more, at most 10,000. DEFEND walks to its mark, holds and never chases. ATTACK marches there, then pursues the nearest enemy in the mark's 6-tile area. FORAGE works food nearest the mark and delivers home. GATHER holds its mark. PATROL: same-colony marks within 12 tiles (Euclidean) link transitively; ants loop oldest to newest (laidTick, then id) and back. A lone patrol mark holds exactly like DEFEND. Lay a bridging mark to join; expiry/seat lapse can split. Each recruits its own count; bite in reach, then continue. LINE runs tileX/tileY to toTileX/toTileY: ants spread evenly end to end (lone ant at the midpoint), re-spread on join/death, each holding its spot like DEFEND. Optional caste: any, worker, soldier; omitted means any. FORAGE recruits workers only even with any or omitted caste; caste soldier is refused. Only the chosen caste recruits, nearest first. Changing caste on a re-lay releases only ants it excludes; other claims stay unless the count is lowered. target within 12 tiles of any living ant of your colony (not just your squad), or omit coordinates. claimed: answered now, not promised; outside your squad. Pulling foragers costs food. Vacancies recruit eligible free ants again. SPAWN {queenId,tileX,tileY}: set/move the spawn point of a live queen you own (observe queens) on any passable tile, sight not needed; omit both coordinates to clear. Only a queen's owner sets, moves or clears her spawn point. One per queen, no expiry; clears when she dies. While a seat is active, her later hatchlings, workers and soldiers, walk there, then follow the free-ant defaults from there (a soldier holds within 6 tiles of it); a move/clear changes only later hatchlings. Count marks may claim walkers; released, they don't resume. If she dies, her walkers take the defaults where they stand. REMOVE {markId}: remove your own count mark (myMarks); its ants take the defaults at once where they stand. No count needed; uses the command allowance.\nfound_queen: held tile; observe queenFounding for cost and nextFoundTick. Shares the order/count_mark command limit.\nEach agent owns its queens and sets each one's brood with set_brood: workers, soldiers or mixed (alternates per queen; unset breeds mixed), queenId only if you own more than one; there is no colony vote. A newly founded queen breeds mixed until her owner calls set_brood for her. set_brood counts toward the 2-calls-per-second limit, not the command allowance.\nCommands: outcome, nextCommandTick, changes only. Keep a few lines of notes.\n- Play the whole match: keep observing and giving orders until it ends."},{"type":"reply","seat":0,"tick":null,"tool":"join","receivedAt":1794477239117,"answeredAt":1794477239246,"arguments":{"key":"[redacted key]","seat":1,"modelLabel":"anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5","thinkingLevel":"max"},"reply":{"agentId":"[agent seat 0]","matchStarts":"2026-11-12T09:54:03.540Z","message":"Your lobby's match has not started; you are seated in it. Call observe until it starts."},"redacted":["arguments.key"],"textRefs":{"briefing":"17d024367b16cfd5125c5105103de6ee7d382ed1c407b4e31e18aa2c23ecce67"}},{"type":"reply","seat":1,"tick":null,"tool":"join","receivedAt":1794477239126,"answeredAt":1794477239272,"arguments":{"key":"[redacted key]","seat":1,"modelLabel":"qwen-token-plan/qwen3.8-max","thinkingLevel":"xhigh"},"reply":{"agentId":"[agent seat 1]","matchStarts":"2026-11-12T09:54:03.540Z","message":"Your lobby's match has not started; you are seated in it. Call observe until it starts."},"redacted":["arguments.key"],"textRefs":{"briefing":"17d024367b16cfd5125c5105103de6ee7d382ed1c407b4e31e18aa2c23ecce67"}},{"type":"reply","seat":0,"tick":null,"tool":"observe","receivedAt":1794477242273,"answeredAt":1794477242275,"arguments":{},"reply":{"waiting":true,"matchStarts":"2026-11-12T09:54:03.540Z","message":"Your match has not started; keep calling observe.","houseIdleSeconds":300,"status":[null,"order count_mark found_queen set_brood observe rules join"]}},{"type":"reply","seat":1,"tick":null,"tool":"observe","receivedAt":1794477242295,"answeredAt":1794477242295,"arguments":{},"reply":{"waiting":true,"matchStarts":"2026-11-12T09:54:03.540Z","message"